WEBVTT

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.280
<b>Drugstore</b>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.280
<b>In Another World</b>

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.190
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.190
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 1
Stuck-In-Place Super Glue</b>

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.190
I'm back.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.200
Wh-What was that?!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.140
Woof.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.170
Woof.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.540
Ms. Noela, it's dangerous to 
swing a knife at full strength.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.910
Mina, not full strength. 10% strength.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.480
Why are you so pleased with yourself?

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.470
What did I tell you? 
Ms. Noela, you broke another knife!

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.790
Mr. Reiji will be upset when 
he finds out about this!

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.310
Woof!

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.510
Sorry, Mina. Sorry.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.240
It's a secret. Don't tell Master.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.380
We have spare knives. 
Master won't know I broke it.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.820
That knife you broke just 
now was our spare knife.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.490
Woof?!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.950
What am I going to do?
I won't be able to cook today.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.200
Woof...

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.210
Moping cutely won't do you any good.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.210
Is something wrong?

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.500
Oh, Mr. Reiji.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.380
Listen to this. Ms. Noela—

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.380
Master!

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.790
Mina is angry.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.880
Yes, because—

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.640
I know, I know. I was watching.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.550
Noela broke a knife, right?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.680
Woof?!

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.910
Master, are you mad?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.100
I wouldn't get angry over a knife or two.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.520
Woof!

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.650
Jeez. Mr. Reiji, you always baby her.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.840
In any case, I won't be able to cook now.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.270
That's a problem for me, too.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.900
Could you go buy another 
knife at the tool shop?

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.950
Well, not being able to cook 
dinner is a big problem.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.870
I'll go with you!

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.630
<i>Noela is as carefree as ever.</i>

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.830
Is this the right way?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.410
We're going to the tool shop.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.960
Tool shop? Why are you going there, Master?

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.800
<i>I knew it. She forgot.</i>

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.760
I remember now! A knife!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.630
Looks like this is the place.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.740
Woof.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.410
Let's go inside.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.230
Woof.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.620
It's so dark.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.610
This place is filthy.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.990
Is this store even open?

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.080
Master, I want this!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.870
Hup.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.490
Ta-da! How do I look, Master?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.000
You can hardly stand.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:58.830
Woof...

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.300
Let's see...

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.090
Found them.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.550
Let's see... Hello!

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.020
I'd like to buy a knife.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.380
Excuse me... I need a knife.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.250
Excuse me!

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.160
Excuse me!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.580
Oh, shut up!

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.890
H-Hello?

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.880
Hello, woof?

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.560
Shut up. Stop shouting at me.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.710
I'm drowning in repairs.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.400
When I woke up, I found 
myself lying on the floor.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.760
Repairs?

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.500
Hey, are you that alchemist 
everyone's been talking about?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.560
I'm a pharmacist.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.150
Woof.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:17.080
<b>Paula</b>

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:15.370
I'm Paula. As you can see, I run this shop.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.080
<i>"As you can see"?</i>

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.500
A-Anyway, nice to meet you.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.840
Nice to meet you.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.150
You're busy with repairs?

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.930
<i>So</i> busy.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.140
You know, I drink your enerpos every night.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.100
They're a lifesaver. Thank you.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:40.100
Enerpos? Oh, you mean my energy potions.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.780
That's right. I've been asked to repair 
the Red Cat Brigade's armor on top of

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.240
what the townsfolk have asked me to do.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.550
I'm so sleepy.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.240
So you've been pulling all-nighters.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:56.090
These gauntlets have been giving me trouble.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.710
They belong to the beautiful 
and awesome captain.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:04.420
Ms. Annabelle? Oh, I see 
this iron plate is broken.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:11.170
She protects the town by fighting bandits, 
capturing robbers, and subduing drunkards.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.370
I appreciate everything Ms. Annabelle does.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.630
This goes... here.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.810
This goes... here?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.980
This looks like a lot of work.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.910
How do you fix them?

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:28.140
By patching them up with leather 
or using iron to mend them.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:31.580
The toughest jobs are iron plates 
that have broken in half and

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:36.490
can't be repaired no matter how 
hard I try, like these gauntlets.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:41.330
I wish they'd buy new ones, but they ask 
me to repair what they have instead.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.450
These jobs take up the most time.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:47.800
Well, the Red Cat Brigade 
is a poor mercenary company.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.480
Rei, can't you make some kind 
of incredible liquid that

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.230
fixes things just by sticking 
broken parts in it?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.990
"Rei"?

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:04.280
I can't make the kind of 
magic tool you're asking for.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.690
Sticking?

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.010
Sticking... sticking...

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.370
Wait, I may be able to make something!

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.090
What? Really?!

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:16.990
Give me a minute!

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.790
Bring it on, Demon King! I'll make you cry!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.280
Werewolves are strong! Woof, woof, woof!

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:27.000
Take one critical hit, and two, 
and three, and four...

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:28.200
That's it, Noela the Hero! Show no mercy!

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:35.100
Oh, welcome... back...

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.050
Here, your knives.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.190
Thank you. Now I can cook 
us a delicious dinner.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.500
Okay, it's done!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.850
See you later.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.960
Paula, it's do—

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:17.100
Paula, wake up. It's done. 
You'll able to fix things quickly with this.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:24.440
Huh? What? Rei, you made it already?

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.300
Wow...

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.400
Yes.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.590
No way!

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.140
This'll fix things quickly?

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.760
Yeah. Watch this.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:41.380
It stuck together! What?!

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:46.040
How? How? How?! That only took a second! Wow!

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.950
Pull as hard as you can!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:04.690
<b>Stuck-In-Place Super Glue</b>

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.930
<i>Stuck-In-Place Super Glue.</i>

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:04.690
<i>A liquid that attaches objects 
with tremendous adhesive strength.</i>

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:08.750
I-I can't pull it apart at all. 
What is this? It's friggin' incredible.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.200
R-Right?

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.570
Great. Now Ms. Annabelle can 
fight as hard as she wants.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.250
I'll be able to work so much faster now!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.690
Thanks, Rei!

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.280
Sure thing. Huh?

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.560
Woof.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.950
Woof, woof.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.500
H-Hey, that's—

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.700
Woof? Woof?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.310
Woof! They're stuck together! Woof!

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:34.840
Don't do that!

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.390
Master, disaster!

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.470
Yeah, I know.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.100
Those'll be stuck together for a while.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:49.230
Okay, okay. I know. Let's head home for now.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.900
Hey, wait! Noela, d-don't tell me you...

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.490
It won't come off!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.710
It won't come off. I'm stuck to Master.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.870
Don't you dare sparkle at me!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.320
Rei, I'll stop by to thank you later!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.400
Got it.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.180
Welcome back.

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:21.350
Why are you holding hands?

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.530
I'm stuck to Master because of the medicine.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.770
We'll be together forever!

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.280
Woof.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:31.280
What? That's what happened?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:35.620
D-Does that mean you'll have to bathe, 
use the bathroom, and go to bed together?

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:36.780
I guess so.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.830
Bathing, bathroom, and bed together.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.100
We'll be together while bathing 
and using the bathroom, too.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.700
We'll see everything.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:46.870
Woof.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.830
<i>Does that mean she's okay with it?</i>

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.290
What?!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:53.130
Y-You can't do that! It's indecent!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.370
You'll even be sleeping in the same b-b-bed!

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.380
Don't do anything dirty!

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.600
Not dirty. You're dirty for thinking that.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.680
Mina, you're the dirtiest of all.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:07.420
Oh, no!

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.720
Mina, what were you imagining?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.100
Huh?!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:16.070
Dirty thoughts. Mina was 
thinking dirty thoughts.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.190
I was not!

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.130
Oh, so that's why.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:23.570
Even though you're telling us it's 
wrong, you're the dirtiest one here.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.290
You're bullying me!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:31.450
Yes, that's right! I have a 
dirty mind! Are you satisfied?

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:30.300
Maybe we teased her a bit too much.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:37.220
This is impossible to do 
one-handed! Noela, hold still!

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:38.420
Woof, woof!

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:41.430
Okay, it's done.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.600
<i>Stuck No More Releasing Agent.</i>

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:48.890
<b>Stuck No More Releasing Agent</b>

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.890
<i>A liquid that weakens 
powerful adhesive forces.</i>

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:53.310
No, no! I won't be stuck to Master anymore!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.600
Hey, hold still!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:03.950
It came off. But we were one...

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.810
Noela, from now on, don't go 
touching medicines you don't—

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:03.950
She's not listening.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.410
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.410
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:09.750
Thank you.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.950
Yesterday was a disaster.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.240
Welco—

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.970
<i>Who is this woman?</i>

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.740
<i>Glasses and blue hair?</i>

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.080
U-Um...

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:58.000
Because of you, Rei, I was able to 
get plenty of sleep today. Thanks.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.670
Are you Paula?!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:01.090
Yeah.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.350
What?!

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.610
What, did you forget about me?

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.220
No, I just didn't recognize you.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.930
What?!

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.470
<i>She looks totally different!</i>

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:20.570
After that, I was able to finish the work 
I thought would take me a whole month,

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.060
all because of that stuff!

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.040
That medicine is amazing!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.680
And so are you for making it so quickly!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.080
Here's your payment.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:31.990
This much?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.270
This is too much.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:35.790
I'll stop by again when I'm free.

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:37.660
See you later.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:45.020
Stop by again? She wouldn't...

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:48.770
<i>I had no idea she meant she'd 
be coming over every day.</i>

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:53.350
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.350
Woof, woof.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.350
<b>3 Days Later</b>

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:59.100
It's not that those people 
don't come to my shop.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:59.100
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 2
Glossy Shine Polish</b>

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:03.010
"Those people"? You mean adventurers?

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:06.260
Yeah. They come to my shop,

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:10.770
but they look at my merchandise 
and then leave immediately.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:16.330
It's written all over their faces. They think 
it's just a shoddy countryside tool shop.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.560
Ms. Paula, welcome.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:23.800
Thanks. Mina, you're 
looking cute again today.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.720
Oh, please.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.430
Paula, you're like a middle-aged man.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.730
Hey, wanna hang out after work?

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:35.970
Could you not hit on my employees?

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:41.840
Mr. Reiji, should I serve some tea?

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.400
No need. She'll be leaving soon.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.320
Rei, don't be like that.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:51.350
We're both shopkeepers. I'm sure 
there's plenty we could discuss.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:56.200
There really isn't. I've run out of things 
to say since you've been coming every day.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:01.210
You know, I've got plenty of good 
merchandise, too, Rei! But they...

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.060
You're still talking? You do 
whatever you want, don't you?

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.170
If you look closely, you'll find that 
I've got a decent selection of tools.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.670
But they leave without taking a good look.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:13.330
Your shop is just dark overall.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:17.020
It feels less like a tool shop 
and more like an antique shop.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.670
What?! That's not true!

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.100
I keep my merchandise polished!

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.530
And it's still that dark?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.570
<i>How is she polishing that stuff?</i>

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:31.390
Wanna come over? Wanna come? 
Wanna check things out?

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.030
Guess I don't have a choice.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.990
Yeah, your store is too dark.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:39.210
You think so? I think this is normal.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:41.960
You've gotten used to it because 
you're here all the time.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:46.290
This is why adventurers who 
stop by leave immediately.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.210
Really? You think so?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.720
Wh-What?!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.370
I-It burns...

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.370
Are you a vampire?!

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:58.370
Are you a child?!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:15:59.420
Just kidding.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:04.060
But it is a little brighter now, Rei.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:04.740
Right?

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.850
If you could just handle the 
rest, that would be great.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.830
Hold on. You're doing this, too.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.830
All of it!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:14.280
"Too"? You mean you'll help me, Rei?

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.930
<i>I shouldn't have said that.</i>

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:20.200
I need employees, don't I?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.160
I'd like someone cute, like Mina.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.310
You can't have Mina.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:25.730
What about Noela, then?

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:26.990
You can't have Noela, either.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.590
Aww...

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.550
Fine, then. I'll guess you'll do.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:34.880
Why are you acting like you 
just have no other choice?

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:39.160
You should look elsewhere for employees.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.920
But there aren't any cute girls.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.980
Then why did you try to recruit me?!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.320
Because we could enjoy 
chatting about shopkeeping.

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:47.630
How?!

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:52.800
See? Doesn't your shop feel bigger now?

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.610
It does! It's kind of bright, too!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.210
All right, let's get this place cleaned up!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.700
Yeah!

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.460
I let her talk me into cleaning again.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.370
Let's get cleaning!

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.790
It looks a little dark.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:15.260
The color must've dulled since 
it's been on the shelf for so long.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.300
Do you polish these?

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:20.260
Rude! There's no dust on them, is there?

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:23.270
I polish them with oil once a week!

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:25.480
Once a week?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.310
<i>It's covered with small scratches.</i>

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:31.830
<i>She might be able to sell 
this if she kept it cleaner.</i>

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.370
Kept it cleaner?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.290
Hey, we're cleaning! 
Where are you going, alchemist?

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.910
<i>I'm not an alchemist!</i>

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.520
Okay, it's done!

00:17:53.520 --> 00:18:00.180
<b>Glossy Shine Polish</b>

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.410
<i>Glossy Shine Polish.</i>

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:59.730
<i>A liquid that polishes away small scratches.</i>

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:06.060
I'm glad you're back. Once you start 
cleaning, it can be hard to stop.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.350
Try polishing your merchandise with this.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.230
What's this?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.230
Try it.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.190
Okay.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:23.580
Wow, it's so clean!

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.220
Look, Rei!

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:26.290
It looks totally different.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.200
This is insane! This is an 
incredible invention, Rei!

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:32.860
It made this cuirass super clean!

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:35.740
Rei, I think I can sell this now.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:40.280
This will make people stop calling it 
a shoddy countryside tool shop.

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:43.440
It's no wonder people called your shop 
shoddy, considering your merchandise.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.630
Did you say something?

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:46.640
I think I'll polish something, too.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.140
I've been thinking...

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.960
I'm not sure how I feel about a girl 
saying "friggin'" all the time.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.210
Don't sweat the small stuff.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.340
This is friggin' amazing! Friggin' wow!

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:05.870
It's so friggin' clean! Friggin' amazing!

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:11.600
Friggin' wow, friggin' clean, friggin' amazing!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:10.640
That should do it.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:16.190
Master, Master, Master...

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.760
Wrong store.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.500
All right!

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:28.180
I'll definitely get a lot of business now!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:30.890
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:30.410
<i>One week later...</i>

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:36.230
We need to do something to attract 
more adventurers to town.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:42.160
My shop's all clean now, 
but no adventurers are coming.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.370
I see.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.870
Adventurers don't come to 
this town in the first place.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:52.170
Well, we are way out in the countryside. 
We don't have any shrines or caves.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.580
We should build a dungeon.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.560
You can handle that, right, Rei?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.630
What do you think a pharmacist does?

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:06.930
You just thought I'm a pain 
in the butt, didn't you?

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.890
Just now? I've thought that for a while.

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:11.950
Huh?

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.520
<i>That was kind of funny.</i>

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.170
I'm kidding. It was just a joke.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:20.980
I'm sure you'll be able to sell your 
goods once some adventurers show up.

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.960
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.120
<i>Uh-oh. I guess I shouldn't tease 
her about that anymore.</i>

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.520
You felt a little bad about what 
you said just now, didn't you?

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.160
What? Nope.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:38.890
You're lying. You totally 
friggin' thought that.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.590
You're too easy, Rei.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:42.510
I didn't think that! Jeez, you're a pain!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.220
<b>Closing Time</b>

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.640
Kirio Drugstore.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:46.800
Thank you...

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.760
...for visiting...

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:51.180
...again today.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.640
Woof!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:21:00.650
Demon King, I acquired more of 
that medicine from the human town.

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:10.390
As usual, it's criminally delicious.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:11.790
You only bought one?

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.950
I thought I ordered you to buy two.

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:21.800
Demon King, th-the truth is, you seem to 
be hooked on these energy potions lately.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.950
I'm concerned you're drinking too many.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:25.650
Drinking too many?

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:27.320
I mean... it's a medicine.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:31.260
We don't know what side effects it 
could have. If you became addicted—

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.850
That! Doesn't! Matter!

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:40.730
How dare you ignore the orders of the 
almighty ruler of Hell, Demon King Ejil?!

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:46.980
I sentence you to three days of 
imprisonment. Guards, take him away.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.620
Demon King, have mercy!

00:21:50.650 --> 00:21:51.950
Now, then...

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:59.690
The almighty ruler of Hell, Demon King Ejil,

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.960
will have to acquire these potions in person.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Illustration by:</b>
